# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command copflow
usage 1   copflow on [<size>]           start logging coprocessor register-window traffic
usage 2   copflow off                   stop logging
usage 3   copflow clear                 forget everything logged so far
usage 4   copflow tail [<n>]            the last <n> accesses in order (default 20)
usage 5   copflow stats                 per-register read/write tallies, busiest first
usage 6   copflow poll                  the longest run of unchanging reads - a stuck handshake

case the fake target's register window
target fake
covers 1-6
$ copflow
out 43
Usage: copflow on|off|clear|tail|stats|poll
status 0
action none
$ copflow on
out 69
Coprocessor register flow logging on (4096 registers, 4096 retained).
status 0
action none
$ copflow tail
out 96
Nothing logged yet - the cartridge has not touched its coprocessor registers since `copflow on`.
status 0
action none
$ copflow stats
out 96
Nothing logged yet - the cartridge has not touched its coprocessor registers since `copflow on`.
status 0
action none
$ copflow poll
out 96
Nothing logged yet - the cartridge has not touched its coprocessor registers since `copflow on`.
status 0
action none
$ copflow on 10
out 67
Coprocessor register flow logging on (16 registers, 4096 retained).
status 0
action none
$ copflow tail 5
out 96
Nothing logged yet - the cartridge has not touched its coprocessor registers since `copflow on`.
status 0
action none
$ copflow clear
out 38
Coprocessor register flow log cleared.
status 0
action none
$ copflow off
out 38
Coprocessor register flow logging off.
status 0
action none
$ copflow frob
out 68
Unknown copflow subcommand 'frob'. Try on|off|clear|tail|stats|poll.
status 0
action none
end

case a bare target
target bare
covers 1
$ copflow on
out 55
GOLDEN exposes no coprocessor register window to watch.
status 0
action none
end

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ copflow on
out 65
Error: No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
end

case a clear after off
target fake
covers 1-4
$ copflow on
out 69
Coprocessor register flow logging on (4096 registers, 4096 retained).
status 0
action none
$ copflow off
out 38
Coprocessor register flow logging off.
status 0
action none
$ copflow clear
out 38
Coprocessor register flow log cleared.
status 0
action none
$ copflow tail
out 71
Coprocessor register flow logging is off. Turn it on with `copflow on`.
status 0
action none
end
